   9. Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning Training.

      a. No Training.

      Subject to Section 8(a), You may not exercise the Licensed Rights in the
      Licensed Material, in whole or in part, for purposes of Training an
      Artificial Intelligence or Machine Learning Model.

      For purposes of this Section:

      1. "Artificial Intelligence or Machine Learning Model" means a
      computational model or system that uses machine-learning,
      neural-network, statistical-learning, or similar techniques to develop
      learned parameters, weights, representations, or other learned state
      from data.

      2. "Training" means using the Licensed Material, or information derived
      from the Licensed Material, to create, train, pretrain, retrain,
      fine-tune, instruction-tune, optimize, distill, or otherwise modify the
      parameters, weights, representations, or other learned state of an
      Artificial Intelligence or Machine Learning Model.

      Training includes, without limitation:

         A. initial training or pretraining;

         B. continued or additional pretraining;

         C. fine-tuning or instruction-tuning;

         D. supervised, semi-supervised, self-supervised, or unsupervised
         training;

         E. reinforcement learning, including reinforcement learning based on
         human, machine, or other feedback;

         F. model distillation, knowledge transfer, or similar processes in
         which the Licensed Material is used to train or modify another model;

         G. inclusion of the Licensed Material in a dataset, corpus, or
         collection prepared or intended for use in any activity described in
         this Section 9(a);

         H. using the Licensed Material to generate, label, select, rank,
         filter, transform, or otherwise produce synthetic or derived data
         that is subsequently used in any activity described in this Section
         9(a); or

         I. using evaluation, testing, benchmarking, feedback, annotations, or
         other information generated from or with reference to the Licensed
         Material where such information is subsequently used to train,
         fine-tune, optimize, reinforce, distill, or otherwise modify an
         Artificial Intelligence or Machine Learning Model.

      The restrictions in this Section apply regardless of whether the
      Training is commercial or NonCommercial; whether the Licensed Material
      constitutes a substantial or insubstantial portion of the relevant
      dataset, corpus, or training process; whether the Training is performed
      directly or through one or more intermediaries; and whether the
      resulting model is publicly released, privately deployed, or not
      released.

      b. Permitted Artificial Intelligence Assisted Use.

      Section 9(a) does not prohibit use of the Licensed Material as input or
      context to an Artificial Intelligence or Machine Learning Model solely
      for inference, analysis, or other processing that does not result in
      Training as defined in Section 9(a).

      Without limitation, the following uses are permitted, subject to the
      other terms and conditions of this Public License:

      1. submitting the Licensed Material, or a portion thereof, to an
      artificial-intelligence assistant for explanation, summarization,
      analysis, review, translation, debugging, or modification;

      2. asking an artificial-intelligence assistant questions regarding the
      Licensed Material;

      3. using an artificial-intelligence coding assistant in connection with
      development, review, debugging, or modification of the Licensed
      Material;

      4. creating embeddings, indexes, or retrieval systems used to identify
      or supply relevant portions of the Licensed Material as context for
      inference, provided that such embeddings, indexes, or retrieval systems
      are not used for Training; and

      5. using the Licensed Material to evaluate, test, or benchmark an
      Artificial Intelligence or Machine Learning Model, provided that such
      evaluation, testing, or benchmarking does not itself result in Training
      and the resulting evaluation, testing, benchmarking, feedback,
      annotations, or other information is not subsequently used for Training
      as defined in Section 9(a).

      c. Collection for Training.

      You may not exercise the Licensed Rights to scrape, crawl, download,
      reproduce, aggregate, compile, or otherwise collect the Licensed
      Material for inclusion in a dataset, corpus, or collection where the
      purpose of that dataset, corpus, or collection is Training prohibited by
      Section 9(a).

      d. Condition of Licensed Rights.

      Compliance with this Section 9 is an express condition of the Licensed
      Rights granted under this Public License.
